  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BOL100292 Wildfires in Bolivia Alert 873</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Consortium led by Plan with Save the Children and World Vision as partners, addressing critical needs in health, food security, WASH, and protection for vulnerable groups, including Indigenous communities, women, and children. _x000d_
1) WASH: To guarantee the access to safe water and address the contamination of water sources through distribution of safe water through tanker trucks, delivery of water filters, storage tanks, and/or purification tablets to households, schools and producers; rehabilitation of damaged water systems; distribution of hygiene kits, including soap, menstrual hygiene products, and sanitation supplies; hygiene promotion _x000d_
2) Protection: Child-friendly spaces will be established/equipped; measures to prevent gender-based violence (GBV) by offering providing psychosocial services to girls, adolescents and women; protection _x000d_
3) Food security: Emergency food distributions to support families who have lost crops and livestock.</narrative>
  </description>
